[{"id":"fm-core2-2.58-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>For each of the following curves <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> shown below, sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{f(x)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/questions/assets/diagrams/258/q1a_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/questions/assets/diagrams/258/q1b_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/questions/assets/diagrams/258/q1c_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\text{Minimum of }f(x)\\text{ at }(0,-4)\\text{ becomes local maximum of }\\frac{1}{f(x)}\\text{ at }\\left(0,-\\frac14\\right).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{1}{f(x)}\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{1}{f(x)}\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}x\\to-2^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,&amp;x\\to-2^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,\\\\x\\to2^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to2^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty.\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\text{Minimum of }f(x)\\text{ at }\\left(\\frac32,-\\frac94\\right)\\text{ becomes local maximum of }\\frac1{f(x)}\\text{ at }\\left(\\frac32,-\\frac49\\right).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}x\\to0^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,&amp;x\\to0^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,\\\\x\\to3^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to3^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty.\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\text{Maximum of }f(x)\\text{ at }\\left(-\\frac12,\\frac94\\right)\\text{ becomes local minimum of }\\frac1{f(x)}\\text{ at }\\left(-\\frac12,\\frac49\\right).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^-\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^-\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}x\\to-2^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to-2^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,\\\\x\\to1^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,&amp;x\\to1^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty.\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.58-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Sketch each of the following, labelling any local maxima or minima with their coordinates:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{3x-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{(x-4)(x+3)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{2x^2+3x-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{4+3x-x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac1{12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The minimum of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(x-4)(x+3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence the maximum of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1{(x-4)(x+3)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac12,-\\frac4{49}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The minimum of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2x^2+3x-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-\\frac34\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence the maximum of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1{2x^2+3x-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(-\\frac34,-\\frac8{25}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\text{Maximum of }y=4+3x-x^2\\text{ is at }x=\\frac32,\\quad\\text{so the minimum of }y=\\frac1{4+3x-x^2}\\text{ is at }\\left(\\frac32,\\frac4{25}\\right).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.58-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>For each of the following curves <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> shown below, sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{f(x)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/questions/assets/diagrams/258/q3a_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/questions/assets/diagrams/258/q3b_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/questions/assets/diagrams/258/q3c_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^-\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}x\\to-2^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to-2^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,\\\\x\\to-1^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,&amp;x\\to-1^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,\\\\x\\to2^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to2^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty.\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^-\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}x\\to-1^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,&amp;x\\to-1^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,\\\\x\\to0^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to0^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,\\\\x\\to2^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,&amp;x\\to2^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty.\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^-\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}x\\to-1^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,&amp;x\\to-1^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,\\\\x\\to0^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to0^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty.\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.58-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Sketch each of the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{x(x-1)(x-2)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{2x^3-9x^2+3x+4}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{8-2x-5x^2-x^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{x^3+x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^-\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}x\\to0^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to0^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,\\\\x\\to1^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,&amp;x\\to1^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,\\\\x\\to2^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to2^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty.\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2x^3-9x^2+3x+4=(2x+1)(x-1)(x-4).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^-\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}x\\to-\\frac12^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to-\\frac12^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,\\\\x\\to1^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,&amp;x\\to1^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,\\\\x\\to4^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to4^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty.\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"8-2x-5x^2-x^3=-(x-1)(x+2)(x+4).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac18\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^-\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}x\\to-4^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,&amp;x\\to-4^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,\\\\x\\to-2^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to-2^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,\\\\x\\to1^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,&amp;x\\to1^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty.\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^3+x^2=x^2(x+1).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^-\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}x\\to-1^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to-\\infty,&amp;x\\to-1^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,\\\\x\\to0^- &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty,&amp;x\\to0^+ &amp;: \\frac1{f(x)}\\to\\infty.\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.58-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>Each of the following curves are of the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{ax^2+bx+c}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers. Determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/questions/assets/diagrams/258/q5a_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/questions/assets/diagrams/258/q5b_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1{k(x-1)(x-2)}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac32,-\\frac25\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" -\\frac25=\\frac1{k\\left(\\frac32-1\\right)\\left(\\frac32-2\\right)}\\quad\\therefore\\quad k=10.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"10(x-1)(x-2)=10x^2-30x+20,\\qquad y=\\frac1{10x^2-30x+20}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore a=10,\\quad b=-30,\\quad c=20.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1{k(x+1)(x-3)}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,\\frac18)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac18=\\frac1{k(1+1)(1-3)}\\quad\\therefore\\quad k=-2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-2(x+1)(x-3)=-2x^2+4x+6,\\qquad y=\\frac1{-2x^2+4x+6}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore a=-2,\\quad b=4,\\quad c=6.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.58-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>The following curve is of the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{ax^3+bx^2+cx+d}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers. Determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/questions/assets/diagrams/258/q6_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1{k(x+1)(x-1)(x-2)}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,\\frac12)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac12=\\frac1{k(0+1)(0-1)(0-2)}\\quad\\therefore\\quad k=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(x+1)(x-1)(x-2)=x^3-2x^2-x+2,\\qquad y=\\frac1{x^3-2x^2-x+2}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore a=1,\\quad b=-2,\\quad c=-1,\\quad d=2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.58-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Sketch the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{f(x)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\dfrac{x^2+4x}{x^2-4x-5}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac1{f(x)}=\\frac{x^2-4x-5}{x^2+4x}=\\frac{(x+1)(x-5)}{x(x+4)}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Asymptotes: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^2-4x-5=0\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=5,\\ x=-1,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so the intercepts are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. There is no vertical intercept. As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y&lt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y&gt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x\\to-4^-: y\\to+\\infty,\\quad x\\to-4^+:y\\to-\\infty,\\quad x\\to0^-:y\\to+\\infty,\\quad x\\to0^+:y\\to-\\infty.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.58-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>For each of the following curves <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> shown below, sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{f(x)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/questions/assets/diagrams/258/q8a_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/questions/assets/diagrams/258/q8b_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Sketch of the reciprocal curve shown in the printed worked solution.</p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/solutions/assets/diagrams/258/s8a_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Sketch of the reciprocal curve shown in the printed worked solution.</p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/solutions/assets/diagrams/258/s8b_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.58-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>The following curve is of the form</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{1}{ax\\ln(bx)},\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are non-zero integer constants to be found. The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2e},-\\dfrac{e}{4}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. There are asymptotes at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\dfrac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.58/questions/assets/diagrams/258/q9_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<p>Asymptotes at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\ln(bx)=0\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad bx=1\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=\\frac1b\\quad\\therefore\\quad b=2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1{ax\\ln(2x)}\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad -\\frac e4=\\frac1{a\\left(\\frac1{2e}\\right)\\ln\\left(\\frac2{2e}\\right)}\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad-\\frac e4=\\frac{2e}{-a}\\quad\\therefore\\quad a=8.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore a=8\\text{ and }b=2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]